 Bureau of Mines, and tha \n(United States) Geological Survey, each \nof which exercises functions having a \ndirect and immediate connection with \nthe national defense, are hereby desig­\nnated, pursuant to section 103 (a) of the \nAct, as agencies of the Government in­\ncluded within the definition of the term \n“Department” for the purposes of Title I  \nof the Act.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"16 FR 9927, PDF pages 1-1; para. 1","sha256":"07a1e3bb23691db6f2ff88a8767c4acd5dca518f5bda729d5c1dc6e71f801134","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1951-09-29/pdf/FR-1951-09-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10294#para1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"2. In accordance with section 102 of \nthe Act, the provisions of Title I  of the \nAct shall be applicable to all contracts \nwith the Defense Materials Procurement \nAgency, the Bureau of Mines, and the \n(United States) Geological Survey, re­\nspectively, and related subcontracts, to \nthe extent of the amounts received or \naccrued by a contractor or subcontractor \non or after the first day of October 1951, \nwhether such contracts or subcontracts \nwere made on, before, or after that date.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"16 FR 9927, PDF pages 1-1; para. 2","sha256":"07a1e3bb23691db6f2ff88a8767c4acd5dca518f5bda729d5c1dc6e71f801134","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1951-09-29/pdf/FR-1951-09-29.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10294#para2","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"16 FR 9927, PDF pages 1-1","sha256":"07a1e3bb23691db6f2ff88a8767c4acd5dca518f5bda729d5c1dc6e71f801134","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1951-09-29/pdf/FR-1951-09-29.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 2 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not establish